{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>If there is oppression.</b> Perhaps you will think that there is no guardian over your speech because you see violence in public and there is none to deliver." "<b>And the poor's right.</b> Because a person is obligated to help him, and behold he is oppressed." "<b>And robbery of justice.</b> Construct state, like וגדר אבניו. Or in the feminine form, like the matter of 'greater than this,' or 'in robbery.'" "<b>And watch in the province.</b> Before the eyes of all, and not in the wilderness." "<b>Do not marvel at the matter.</b> That you say: what desire does HaShem have that He does not deliver? Know that there is a guardian who sees this violence, and he is not one — rather they are many, and each one high above high, and guardians many; no man knows their number, for they are high over those whose rank is unequal. And one who knows the sod of HaShem will know that 'high above high' — they are fifty-five. And I cannot explain."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {2 "The phrase 'גדל מזה' is obscure; rendered hyper-literally. The referent is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:45.616862529Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}